From: downstream package maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] text: inspect the next UTF-16 unit for a low surrogate

The leading code unit already matched 0xd800 under mask 0xfffffc00.
Testing that same value against 0xdc00 can never succeed. Inspect the
next unit under the existing length guard before consuming the pair.
This is an upstream-generic correction, not a RISC-V-specific change.

Origin: downstream, official v1.3.3 commit bbd91f0d06a71491691b36330f29dffa4af87ccf
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (no upstream write authorized)
License: MIT (same as affected project source)

--- a/source/plutovg-font.c
+++ b/source/plutovg-font.c
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
         const uint16_t* text = it->text;
         codepoint = text[it->index++];
         if(((codepoint) & 0xfffffc00) == 0xd800) {
-            if(it->index < it->length && (((codepoint) & 0xfffffc00) == 0xdc00)) {
+            if(it->index < it->length && (((text[it->index]) & 0xfffffc00) == 0xdc00)) {
                 uint16_t trail = text[it->index++];
                 codepoint = (codepoint << 10) + trail - ((0xD800u << 10) - 0x10000u + 0xDC00u);
             }
